# Own-wording text for Warlock Zine spells (Kobold Press, Open5e, OGL 1.0a). Class lists come from the source (Open5e v1 dnd_class).
TEXT = {
"Avert Evil Eye": ["Level 1. Touch: for 1 hour advantage on saves against blinded, charmed, cursed and frightened. Once, cancel disadvantage on a d20 roll, which ends the spell.",
 "The target gets slight protection against the evil eye for up to 1 hour. It has advantage on saving throws against being blinded, charmed, cursed and frightened. During the spell it can also cancel disadvantage on one d20 roll it is about to make, but doing so ends the spell."],
"Battle Chant": ["Level 2. Casting 1 minute. Allies you choose within 60 ft add 1 to damage on each hit for 5 minutes. Chanted in unison by several casters, add 2.",
 "You bless allied creatures of your choice in range. Whenever a target lands a hit before the spell ends, it can add 1 to the damage roll. When several casters chant together, the bonus is 2. Higher slots: range +10 ft per slot level above 2nd."],
"Charming Aesthetics": ["Level 3. A group of plants or animals looks harmless and lovely for 1 day. A creature that studies them makes a Wis save or is charmed, with disadvantage on Perception, and saves again to leave their sight.",
 "You make a group of the same plants or animals in range look harmless and attractive. A creature that studies one makes a Wisdom save or is charmed by it until the spell ends or another creature that is not its ally harms it. While charmed and within sight, it has disadvantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks and checks to notice danger. If it tries to leave sight, it makes a second Wisdom save or refuses. It can repeat that save once per minute, and on a success it can leave but stays charmed. Higher slots: one more group per slot level above 4th."],
"Child of Light and Darkness": ["Level 8. Roll d20 at the end of each turn: 1-10 light form, 11-20 dark form. Both: immune to nonmagical weapon damage, attackers have disadvantage. Each form adds immunities, a teleport or a pull-push.",
 "For the duration, roll a d20 at the end of each of your turns. On 1 to 10 you become a humanoid of searing light, on 11 to 20 a humanoid of chilling darkness. In both forms you are immune to bludgeoning, piercing and slashing from nonmagical attacks, and attackers have disadvantage against you. Light Form: you shed bright light in a 60 ft radius and dim light 60 ft further, are immune to fire, resist radiant, and once per turn as a bonus action teleport to a space you see within your light. Darkness Form: you are immune to cold, resist necrotic, and once per turn as a bonus action target up to three Large or smaller creatures within 30 ft, each making a Strength save or being pulled or pushed (your choice) up to 20 ft toward or away from you."],
"Commander's Pavilion": ["Level 3. Touch: a 30 by 30 ft command tent, 20 ft high, with maps, a spyglass, writing gear and other minor items. Lasts 24 hours and renews if recast.",
 "You create a command tent 30 ft by 30 ft with a peak 20 ft high. It holds items a commander might need at a campaign headquarters: area maps, a spyglass, a sandglass, writing materials, code references, history and strategy books, banners, spare uniforms and badges of rank. The minor mundane items vanish when the spell ends. Casting it again on later days keeps the tent for another 24 hours."],
"Eternal Echo": ["Level 3. A commanding voice: undead within 60 ft that fail a Wis save obey you. It overrides prior loyalty and can undo a cleric's Turn Undead.",
 "You gain a portentous voice of compelling power that commands all undead within 60 ft that fail a Wisdom save. This overrides any earlier loyalty to casters such as necromancers or evil priests, and it can cancel the result of a cleric's Turn Undead."],
"Exchanged Knowledge": ["Level 3. 1 hour. Double proficiency on Intelligence checks to recall information. Gain advantage by sacrificing a lore book or passing a Cha save. A failed save ends the spell and gives disadvantage for a week.",
 "You open a conduit to the Castle Library and access hard-to-find information. For the duration, you double your proficiency bonus on Intelligence checks to recall information about any subject. You can also gain advantage on such a check by sacrificing another lore-filled book or succeeding on a Charisma save. On a failed save the spell ends and you have disadvantage on all Intelligence checks to recall information for 1 week. A wish spell ends this effect."],
"Hedgehog Dozen": ["Level 3. Touch: eleven illusory duplicates surround the target for 1 minute. It gains advantage against opponents. Each attack against it rolls d8: on a 1 it hits the target, otherwise it removes a duplicate. Ends when five remain.",
 "Eleven illusory duplicates of the touched creature appear in its space, giving it the look of a dozen arms, shields and weapons, a swarm of overlapping identical figures. They move with the target and mimic its actions, so it is impossible to tell which is real. You can use your action to dismiss them. While surrounded, the creature has advantage against any opponent. Whenever a creature targets it with an attack, roll a d8: on a 1 the attack hits the target, on any other result it removes a duplicate. When only five remain, the spell ends. A creature is unaffected if it cannot see, relies on senses other than sight such as blindsight, or can perceive illusions as false, as with truesight."],
"Inconspicuous Facade": ["Level 4. Casting 1 minute. Make a building look unremarkable or smaller or larger, until dispelled. Intelligence (Investigation) against your DC reveals it.",
 "You make a target building seem much less important or ostentatious. You can give it an unremarkable look or one that blends with nearby buildings, but you cannot add standout features or make it look richer than its neighbors. You can make it look larger or smaller to fit in, but cursory physical inspection reveals it, since a creature passes through extra illusory space or bumps into a seemingly smaller part. A creature can use its action to inspect the building and make an Intelligence (Investigation) check against your spell save DC, and on a success it knows the building is disguised. The spell ends if you dispel it or the building is destroyed."],
"March of the Dead": ["Level 3. Casting 1 minute. Animate one Small or Medium humanoid corpse per caster level as zombie-strength constructs. Command them as a bonus action for up to 24 hours of marching. They cannot guard.",
 "You animate the recently dead to carry them from a battlefield. Choose one corpse of a Medium or Small humanoid per caster level within range. Each rises as a construct that looks like a flesh golem but has a zombie's strength and abilities. Dwarves use it to carry the fallen to clan tombs and deny the bodies to ghouls and necromancers. On each of your turns you can use a bonus action to command all the creatures you made, if within 60 ft. You decide their actions and movement for the next day, but cannot order them to guard. With no orders they only defend themselves. They follow an order and direction of march until they reach the destination or 24 hours pass, when the spell ends and the corpses fall lifeless. To march for another 24 hours, cast the spell on them again before the period ends, which reasserts control over up to 50 creatures without animating new ones. Higher slots: two more constructs per slot level above 3rd, each from a different corpse."],
"Obfuscate Object": ["Cantrip. Bonus action. In dim light, an object up to shortsword size on you or unattended within 10 ft is hidden from view for 1 minute. Advantage on Sleight of Hand to hide it. Two objects at level 5, three at 11, four at 17.",
 "While you are in dim light, you make an object in range unobtrusively hidden from other creatures. For the duration you have advantage on Dexterity (Sleight of Hand) checks to hide it. The object cannot be larger than a shortsword and must be on your person, in your hand, or unattended. You can affect two objects at level 5, three at 11 and four at 17."],
"Order of Revenge": ["Level 3. Touch a weapon or 30 pieces of ammo for 1 hour per caster level: creatures it damages leave an invisible glowing trail. See it with revenge's eye or see invisible. Dispel magic stops a creature's trail.",
 "You imbue a touched weapon or bundle of 30 ammunition with spell energy. A creature damaged by an affected weapon leaves an invisibly glowing trail of its path until the spell ends. You can see the trail by casting revenge's eye or see invisible, and any other caster by casting see invisible. Dispel magic on an affected creature stops it leaving a trail, and the trail fades over the next hour. Higher slots: one more weapon or bundle per slot level above 4th."],
"Putrescent Faerie Circle": ["Level 5. A 20 ft toadstool ring within 60 ft. Con save at your turn start: 4d8 necrotic (half on success). Passing through the ring: Con save or 8d8 poison, poisoned and paralyzed (repeat each turn to end paralysis only).",
 "You create a 20 ft diameter circle of loose toadstools that spew sickly white spores and tarry ooze. At the start of each of your turns, each creature inside makes a Constitution save, taking 4d8 necrotic on a failure or half on a success. A creature that tries to pass through the ring triggers a spore cloud and makes a Constitution save, taking 8d8 poison and becoming poisoned for 1 minute on a failure, or half damage and no poison on a success. A poisoned creature is paralyzed. It repeats the Constitution save at the end of each of its turns to end the paralysis (not the poison)."],
"Reassemble": ["Level 5. Casting 1 hour. Touch an undead (dust and bones suffice) destroyed within 10 hours to restore it with full HP. A -4 penalty to attacks, saves and checks fades by 1 per long rest. Limits for liches, sunlight, fire, acid, holy water and gentle repose.",
 "You touch an undead creature (dust and bones will do) destroyed no more than 10 hours ago. Purple fire surrounds it for 1 round and it returns to life with full hit points. It affects only undead, and cannot restore a lich whose phylactery is destroyed, a vampire destroyed by sunlight, an undead whose remains were destroyed by fire, acid or holy water, or remains under gentle repose. It does not remove magical effects, which return if not removed first. It closes mortal wounds but does not restore missing parts. If the creature lacks parts or organs necessary to live, the spell fails. The reassembly costs a huge burst of necrotic energy: ley line casters within 5 miles sense a great shift in life forces and its direction. The target takes -4 to all attacks, saves and ability checks, reduced by 1 after each long rest."],
"Remove Insulation": ["Level 4. Fortitude save (Con) or the target loses lightning resistance, or takes double lightning damage, for 8 hours. Lightning-immune targets save with advantage and gain only resistance on failing. Higher slots extend it.",
 "A creature in range must succeed on a Fortitude saving throw or become less resistant to lightning. A creature immune to lightning has advantage on the save. On a failure, an immune creature instead gains resistance to lightning for the duration, and a creature with resistance loses it. A creature without resistance that fails takes double lightning damage for the duration. Remove curse or similar magic ends it. Higher slots: slot 6 or higher gives 24 hours, slot 8 or higher removes the advantage of lightning-immune creatures, slot 9 or higher lasts until dispelled."],
"Revenge's Eye": ["Level 2. Touch a creature for 1 hour: it can see the trails left by creatures damaged by weapons affected by your order of revenge. Higher slots: +1 creature per level above 2nd.",
 "You touch a creature's eyes and let it see the trails left by creatures damaged by a weapon you enchanted with order of revenge, and only those. Higher slots: one more creature per slot level above 2nd."],
"Rise of the Green": ["Level 8. Plants in 180 ft come alive for 10 minutes (or grow if none). One tree is a friendly treant. Undergrowth is difficult terrain, creatures make a Str save or are restrained (1d6 each turn). Trees swing for 6d6 (Dex save half).",
 "You give life to plants in range, or create undergrowth and trees if there are none. One tree becomes a treant friendly to you and your companions. It has its own initiative and obeys your verbal commands, and defends itself if you give none. The undergrowth is difficult terrain for your enemies. At the start of each of your turns, creatures on the ground in range make a Strength save or are restrained until the spell ends. A restrained creature can use an action for a Strength (Athletics) check against your spell save DC to free itself, and one still restrained at the start of your turn takes 1d6 bludgeoning. The trees also swing at each enemy in range, which makes a Dexterity save, taking 6d6 bludgeoning on a failure or half on a success. A bonus action lets you recenter the spell on yourself, without growing trees where there were none. Higher slots: at slot 9 another tree becomes a treant, the undergrowth deals +1d6, and the trees deal +2d6."],
"Shadow Adaptation": ["Level 2. 8 hours: immune to shadow corruption, resistance to necrotic damage, and advantage on saves against Strength drain or hit point maximum reduction (shadow Strength Drain, harm).",
 "Your flesh and clothes pale as your body takes a sliver of the Shadow Realm. For the duration you are immune to shadow corruption and resist necrotic damage. You also have advantage on saving throws against effects that reduce your Strength score or hit point maximum, such as a shadow's Strength Drain or the harm spell."],
"Skull Road": ["Level 5. A 5 to 20 ft portal to an imprecise place on the plane of Evermaw for 1 minute. Slot 5 reaches a wild area (up to 7 days to a settlement), slot 7 reaches a small gnoll, ghoul or shadow settlement. Undead casters can open it outward.",
 "You conjure a portal linking an open space you see in range to an imprecise spot on the plane of Evermaw. It is a circle 5 to 20 ft across, oriented as you choose, and lasts for the duration. Cast at 5th level it opens to the River of Tears, the Vitreous Mire or the Plains of Bone in a dark forest, cavern or ruin far from habitation, and travel to a settlement can take up to 7 days (1d6+1). At 7th level it opens near a small settlement of gnolls, ghouls or shadows near the Eternal Palace of Mot or a similar place. Undead casters can use it the other way, opening a portal from Evermaw to the mortal world with similar limits. At 7th level the road leads straight to a tomb, cemetery or mass grave near a humanoid settlement."],
"Storm of Axes": ["Level 4. Conjure axes in a 40 by 5 ft line (or 20 ft by 10 ft): 6d8 slashing, Dex save half. While you concentrate, move them 20 ft per round. Creatures they move into save again for damage.",
 "You conjure dozens of axes in a chopping, whirling pattern filling eight 5 ft squares in a 40 ft line, or in a double-strength line 20 ft long and 10 ft deep. They deal 6d8 slashing to creatures in the area when cast, or half with a successful Dexterity save. By keeping concentration you can move the axes up to 20 ft per round in any direction. If they move into spaces with creatures, those creatures make another Dexterity save or take the damage again."],
"Summon Clockwork Beast": ["Level 5. Casting 10 minutes, once per day. Summon a Tiny clockwork beast for 1 hour. It needs no air, food, drink or sleep and crumbles to gears at 0 HP.",
 "Once per day you can cast this ritual to summon a Tiny clockwork beast. It needs no air, food, drink or sleep. When reduced to 0 hit points it crumbles into gears and springs. The source text is cut short, so check the book for the beast's statistics."],
"Toxic Pollen": ["Level 2. One plant type within 30 ft is primed for 1 year to release a 10 ft radius pollen cloud on conditions you set: Con save or poisoned 1 minute, repeating each turn. Each plant releases once.",
 "One type of plant in range gains the ability to puff a pollen cloud when conditions you state during casting are met. The plant sprays a 10 ft radius sphere centered on it. Creatures in it make a Constitution save or are poisoned for 1 minute, repeating the save at the end of each of their turns to end it. A plant can release its pollen only once during the duration."],
"Vagrant's Nondescript Cloak": ["Level 2. Touch: for 1 hour the target is warded against locate creature. A caster learns only if it is within 1,000 ft, not its direction. If already affected by such a spell, both end. Higher slots: +1 creature per level above 2nd.",
 "You ward a touched creature against locate creature. The caster can tell whether the creature is within 1,000 ft but not the direction to it. If the creature is already affected by one of the warded spells, both that effect and this spell end at once. Higher slots: one more creature per slot level above 2nd."],
"Vengeful Panopy of the Ley Line Ignited": ["Level 6. Bound to a ley line, cloak yourself in heliotropic fire (dim light 10 ft) for 10 minutes. Each round make a ranged spell attack for 6d6 force. Attackers within 5 ft take 3d6 force. Your ley bond weakens every 3 minutes.",
 "While bound to a ley line you draw its power, wrapped in magical heliotropic fire that sheds dim light in a 10 ft radius. Each round, including the one you cast it, you can make a ranged spell attack as an action, dealing 6d6 force on a hit. Every 3 minutes the effect is active, your ley bond drops one step: Titanic becomes Strong, then Weak, and after 10 minutes the bond breaks. The bond's strength returns only after a long rest, and a broken bond can only be restored at the next weaker level for a week. A bond broken from a Weak ley line cannot be restored for two weeks. Some believe the spell damages ley lines. Whenever a creature within 5 ft hits you with a melee attack, the cloak flares and the attacker takes 3d6 force. Higher slots: all damage +1d6 per slot level above 6th."],
"Who Goes There?": ["Level 5. Casting 10 minutes. Sift the air for echoes of recent talk to find passwords or key info. Wisdom (Perception) check against the speaker's Wisdom score (DC 10 if unspecified) to pick the key word.",
 "You sift the air for sound-wave remnants of recent conversations to find passwords or other important information, such as from guards on a picket line. The spell forms a cloud of words in your mind and ranks their relevance. Picking the right word or phrase is not guaranteed, but you can make an educated guess. You make a Wisdom (Perception) check against the target person's Wisdom score (DC 10 if not specified) to pick the key word or phrase."],
"Zymurgic Aura": ["Level 7. A 30 ft radius wave of rot on creatures you choose. Con save: 10d6 necrotic (half on success), and their max HP drops by the damage taken until a long rest.",
 "A wave of putrefaction surges from you toward creatures of your choice within 30 ft, speeding their decay. Each target makes a Constitution save, taking 10d6 necrotic on a failure or half on a success. Its hit point maximum drops by the damage taken, until it takes a long rest."],
}
